            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
          %h2#references References
          %p A general account is for instance in section 9.6 of
          %ul
            %li#May
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Concise+Course+in+Algebraic+Topology"} A Concise Course in Algebraic Topology
          %p The characterization of weak homotopy equivalences by lifts up to homotopy seems is in
          %ul
            %li#Jardine
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"}> J. F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial Presheaves
            %li#Vogt
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"}> Rainer Vogt
                ,
                %em The HELP-Lemma and its converse in Quillen model categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.5249"}> arXiv:1004.5249
                )
          %p For related and general discussion see also section 6.5 of
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p Examples for the non-symmetry of the weak homotopy equivalence relation are in
          %ul
            %li#McCord
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+McCord"}> Michael McCord
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Singular homology groups and homotopy groups of finite topological spaces
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.dmj/1077376525"} euclid.dmj/1077376525
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Topospaces-Wiki,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://topospaces.subwiki.org/wiki/Weak_homotopy_equivalence_of_topological_spaces"} Weak homotopy equivalence of topological spaces
          %p Detection in terms of free homotopy sets:
          %ul
            %li#MatumotoMinamiSugawara84
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Takao+Matumoto"}> Takao Matumoto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Norihiko+Minami"} Norihiko Minami
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masahiro+Sugawara"} Masahiro Sugawara
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the set of free homotopy classes and Brown’s construction
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/hiroshima-mathematical-journal/volume-14/issue-2/On-the-set-of-free-homotopy-classes-and-Browns-construction/10.32917/hmj/1206133043.full"} doi:10.32917/hmj/1206133043
          %p
            The weak homotopy equivalences among
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+connected+topological+space"} path connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
            can be detected by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular
            chain functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_*(X)
            is regarded its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebra"} dg-coalgebra
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Manuel+Rivera"}> Manuel Rivera
